<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>DocUp | Notes, PYQs, Study Material & College Documents</title>

    <meta name="description" content="DocUp helps students discover notes, previous year papers, study material, handwritten PDFs and academic documents across multiple degrees and colleges using a smart Doc Score system.">

    <meta name="keywords" content="notes pdf, previous year papers, college study material, handwritten notes, semester notes, university documents, student notes, docup">

    <link rel="canonical" href="https://docup.in/seo">

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo+Black&family=Saira:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/seo.css">
</head>
<body>

<div class="bg-orb orb-1"></div>
<div class="bg-orb orb-2"></div>
<div class="bg-grid"></div>

<header class="hero">
    <nav class="navbar">
        <div class="logo">DocUp</div>

        <div class="nav-links">
            <a href="/dashboard">Search</a>
            <a href="/uploads">Upload</a>
            <a href="/login">Login</a>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <section class="hero-main">
        <div class="hero-left">
            <div class="hero-badge">Smarter academic document discovery</div>

            <h1>
                Find Notes, PYQs, PDFs and Study Material
                <span>Across Colleges and Degrees</span>
            </h1>

            <p class="hero-text">
                DocUp helps students discover academic documents like handwritten notes,
                previous year question papers, semester material, and useful PDFs from
                real students and real colleges — powered by a smart Doc Score system.
            </p>

            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a href="/dashboard" class="primary-btn">Explore Documents</a>
                <a href="/uploads" class="secondary-btn">Upload Your Notes</a>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-points">
                <div class="point-card">
                    <strong>Doc Score Based</strong>
                    <p>Every user starts with 5 Doc Score and receives 2 more daily.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="point-card">
                    <strong>Built to Expand</strong>
                    <p>Not limited to engineering — designed for multiple degrees and streams.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="point-card">
                    <strong>Community Driven</strong>
                    <p>Documents come from students, making the library practical and relevant.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-right">
            <div class="preview-shell">
                <div class="preview-topbar">
                    <div class="preview-dot"></div>
                    <div class="preview-dot"></div>
                    <div class="preview-dot"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="preview-card preview-search">
                    <div class="mini-label">Search smarter</div>
                    <h3>College + Degree + Subject + Year</h3>
                    <p>Quickly filter through academic documents and discover what actually matters.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="preview-card preview-score">
                    <div class="score-pill">Doc Score</div>
                    <h2>5</h2>
                    <p>Starting credit for new users</p>
                </div>

                <div class="preview-row">
                    <div class="small-preview">
                        <span>Notes</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="small-preview">
                        <span>PYQs</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="small-preview">
                        <span>PDFs</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</header>

<main>

    <section class="section trust-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span class="section-tag">Why DocUp</span>
            <h2>A Better Way to Access Academic Material</h2>
            <p>
                DocUp is built for practical academic discovery — not random clutter.
                Search, score, upload and access useful student documents in one place.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-grid">
            <article class="feature-card">
                <div class="feature-icon">01</div>
                <h3>Doc Score System</h3>
                <p>
                    Instead of unlimited free access, DocUp uses a credit-style Doc Score model.
                    Users start with 5 Doc Score and receive 2 more every day.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="feature-card">
                <div class="feature-icon">02</div>
                <h3>Beyond One Degree</h3>
                <p>
                    DocUp is not restricted to only engineering content. The platform is built
                    to scale across different courses, degrees and academic streams.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="feature-card">
                <div class="feature-icon">03</div>
                <h3>Student-Contributed Resources</h3>
                <p>
                    Real student uploads make the content practical, exam-relevant and closer
                    to what learners actually need.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article class="feature-card">
                <div class="feature-icon">04</div>
                <h3>Search-First Experience</h3>
                <p>
                    Discover notes, question papers and PDFs with filters that make it easier
                    to find relevant documents faster.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section seo-copy-section">
        <div class="content-card">
            <span class="section-tag">Academic document platform</span>
            <h2>Notes, Previous Year Papers, PDFs and Study Material</h2>
            <p>
                DocUp is an academic document platform where students can discover useful notes,
                previous year question papers, handwritten PDFs and college study material.
                The goal is to make academic resources easier to discover while building a more
                structured system around quality, access and contribution.
            </p>
            <p>
                Whether students are searching for semester notes, revision material, PYQs,
                subject-wise PDFs or useful college documents, DocUp is designed to make that
                discovery process cleaner and faster.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-card">
            <span class="section-tag">Built for scale</span>
            <h2>Made for Multiple Degrees and Streams</h2>
            <p>
                DocUp is not meant to stay limited to one academic category. The platform is
                planned to expand across a wide range of degrees, streams and college ecosystems,
                making it useful for a broader student audience over time.
            </p>
            <p>
                That makes DocUp more than a notes website — it becomes a larger academic
                discovery layer for student-driven documents.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-card">
            <span class="section-tag">Smart access model</span>
            <h2>How the Doc Score Model Works</h2>
            <p>
                Access on DocUp is supported through Doc Score. New users begin with 5 Doc Score,
                and 2 additional Doc Score are provided daily. This helps balance document access,
                encourages thoughtful usage and supports a more sustainable content ecosystem.
            </p>
            <p>
                Instead of positioning the platform as completely free, DocUp creates a more
                controlled and scalable way to access academic resources.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section categories-section">
        <div class="section-heading center">
            <span class="section-tag">What users search for</span>
            <h2>Popular Academic Resource Categories</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="category-wrap">
            <div class="category-chip">Semester Notes</div>
            <div class="category-chip">Previous Year Papers</div>
            <div class="category-chip">Handwritten Notes</div>
            <div class="category-chip">College PDFs</div>
            <div class="category-chip">Subject-wise Material</div>
            <div class="category-chip">Exam Preparation Resources</div>
            <div class="category-chip">University Documents</div>
            <div class="category-chip">Student Uploads</div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section cta-section">
        <div class="cta-box">
            <span class="section-tag">Start using DocUp</span>
            <h2>Search smarter. Upload better. Discover faster.</h2>
            <p>
                Explore academic documents, contribute useful notes and make the most of your Doc Score.
            </p>

            <div class="cta-buttons">
                <a href="/dashboard" class="primary-btn">Go to Dashboard</a>
                <a href="/uploads" class="secondary-btn">Upload Documents</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

</main>

<footer class="footer">
    <div class="footer-logo">DocUp</div>
    <p>
        Academic documents, notes, PYQs and student resources — organized for smarter discovery.
    </p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>